From d218d337281fd28a53e3fe0e11afbaf25dd0e75e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:12:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] WebPlayer: type into a page from a keyboard along the bottom

A page in a web view has no way to receive text from a remote: the user
cannot type into its fields without a keyboard attached. When the page
focuses a field and asks for the compositor's keyboard, the client
manager shows a web keyboard dialog on a job thread, derived from the
generic keyboard with its own Estuary layout: the keys in a band along
the bottom, no field of its own, hidden text for passwords. Every
change of the typed text goes to the page at once through the text
input, deleting what was sent before and committing the new text, so
the page's field is the one showing the text. Done and Back both close
the keyboard and leave the text. The dialog is named webkeyboard for
keymaps and falls back to the virtualkeyboard section, so Backspace and
Enter act as they do in Kodi's keyboard. A keyboard with letter keys
attached means the user types into the page directly, so the dialog
stays away then.

The manager keeps the caret rectangle the client reports and, when the
caret lies under the keys, scrolls the page under it by the overlap,
once per caret position; a page that cannot scroll reports the same
caret again and is left alone.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
